"text":"Giveaway by Martin Necas","type":{"id":"1402","text":"Giveaway","abbreviation":"giveaway"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:45"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"17"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4233586","displayName":"Martin Necas","shortName":"M. Necas"},"type":"giver"}]},{"id":"401892536000000850","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Takeaway by Sam Malinski","type":{"id":"1401","text":"Takeaway","abbreviation":"takeaway"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:50"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"17"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5136735","displayName":"Sam Malinski","shortName":"S. Malinski"},"type":"taker"}]},{"id":"401892536000000830","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Jaden Schwartz Wrist Shot saved by Joseph Woll","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:09"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"17"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5835","displayName":"Jaden Schwartz","shortName":"J. Schwartz"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4271575","displayName":"Joseph Woll","shortName":"J. Woll"},"type":"saver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1845","fullName":"Xfinity Mobile Arena","address":{"city":"Philadelphia","state":"PA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1845.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":18353,"officials":[{"fullName":"Frederick L'Ecuyer","displayName":"Frederick L'Ecuyer","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Francis Charron","displayName":"Francis Charron","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Libor Suchanek","displayName":"Libor Suchanek","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Onni Hautamaki","displayName":"Onni Hautamaki","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Matvei Michkov scores 2 goals and Flyers beat Avalanche 3-2 for 2nd straight win","description":"— Matvei Michkov scored two goals and the Philadelphia Flyers beat the Colorado Avalanche 3-2 on Monday night for their second straight victory after opening the season with nine consecutive losses.","story":"PHILADELPHIA -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149170/matvei-michkov\">Matvei Michkov</a> scored two goals and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/col/colorado-avalanche\">Colorado Avalanche</a> 3-2 on Monday night for their second straight victory after opening the season with nine consecutive losses.\n\n\r\n              Michkov leads the Flyers with six goals this season. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3096237/noel-acciari\">Noel Acciari</a> also scored for Philadelphia, which lost six games in regulation and three in overtime or shootouts before breaking through on Saturday with <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/flyers-senators-score-346797d4817a1626b04d391077904e33\">a victory over Ottawa</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4271575/joseph-woll\">Joseph Woll</a> made 24 saves for his first victory with the Flyers. He spent the previous five seasons with Toronto.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233586/martin-necas\">Martin Necas</a> and rookie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5136616/tj-hughes\">T.J. Hughes</a> scored for the Avalanche (5-3-1), last season's Presidents' Trophy winners. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904177/mackenzie-blackwood\">Mackenzie Blackwood</a> stopped 21 shots.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188341/cole-knuble\">Cole Knuble</a> <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/flyers-cole-knuble-nhl-debut-54d378536fc44d169226e05b97d1076b\">made his NHL debut</a> for the Flyers, the team he grew up rooting for. His father, Mike, played for Philadelphia from 2005-09 and in 2013. The 22-year-old right wing had 13 minutes, 44 seconds of ice time.\n\n\r\n              Mitchkov scored on a power play at 7:41 of the first period and made it 2-0 at 12:23 of the second when he skated around the net and <a href=\"https://x.com/NHL/status/2112342717539709403\">fired a long-range wrist shot</a> past several players that beat Blackwood on the glove side.\n\n\r\n              Necas got the Avalanche on the board with 2:08 left in the second. Acciari restored Philadelphia's two-goal lead at 6:34 of the third, the veteran center's first goal as a Flyer.\n\n\r\n              Hughes scored at 14:40 of the third, his second straight game with a goal after he found the net for the first time in Friday's win over Pittsburgh.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Avalanche: At New Jersey on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              Flyers: At Buffalo on Wednesday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-20T01:57:08Z"}}